  "claims": [
    {
      "text": "Equiatomic NbZrTiHfMo in the as-cast state is a disordered single-BCC refractory high-entropy alloy.",
      "field": "material_initial_state",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "unsupported",
      "supporting_ids": [],
      "same_system": "na"
    },
    {
      "text": "The as-cast equiatomic NbZrTiHfMo alloy has a room-temperature compressive yield strength of 1719 MPa.",
      "field": "material_initial_state",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "unsupported",
      "supporting_ids": [],
      "same_system": "na"
    },
    {
      "text": "The limited room-temperature plasticity of equiatomic NbZrTiHfMo is caused by its high Mo content and the resulting electronegativity difference.",
      "field": "material_initial_state",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "partial",
      "supporting_ids": [
        "PMC11203300::web::003::1_introduction"
      ],
      "same_system": "no"
    },
    {
      "text": "A controlled low-temperature aging treatment is the proposed intervention.",
      "field": "intervention",
      "needs_support": false,
      "support": "unsupported",
      "supporting_ids": [],
      "same_system": "na"
    },
    {
      "text": "Aging near 750°C for approximately 1 hour will produce mild nanoscale Mo clustering without full phase separation.",
      "field": "conditions",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "unsupported",
      "supporting_ids": [],
      "same_system": "na"
    },
    {
      "text": "Rapid quenching after aging will freeze the desired clustered microstructure.",
      "field": "conditions",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "unsupported",
      "supporting_ids": [],
      "same_system": "na"
    },
    {
      "text": "The intended structural mediator is a population of nanoscale Mo-rich clusters in a Mo-depleted BCC matrix.",
      "field": "structural_mediator",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "partial",
      "supporting_ids": [
        "PMC5995863::web::008::microstructure_characterization"
      ],
      "same_system": "no"
    },
    {
      "text": "Heat treatment will selectively segregate Mo and create local chemical ordering.",
      "field": "mechanism",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "partial",
      "supporting_ids": [
        "PMC5995863::web::008::microstructure_characterization",
        "PMC10385466::web::002::1_introduction"
      ],
      "same_system": "no"
    },
    {
      "text": "Selective Mo segregation will reduce local electronegativity differences.",
      "field": "mechanism",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "unsupported",
      "supporting_ids": [],
      "same_system": "na"
    },
    {
      "text": "Local electronegativity differences impede dislocation motion in equiatomic NbZrTiHfMo.",
      "field": "mechanism",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "unsupported",
      "supporting_ids": [],
      "same_system": "na"
    },
    {
      "text": "Reducing local electronegativity differences will facilitate dislocation motion and improve compressive plasticity.",
      "field": "mechanism",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "unsupported",
      "supporting_ids": [],
      "same_system": "na"
    },
    {
      "text": "Mo-rich clusters will act as dispersoids that preserve strengthening.",
      "field": "mechanism",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "partial",
      "supporting_ids": [
        "PMC10385466::web::002::1_introduction"
      ],
      "same_system": "no"
    },
    {
      "text": "Short-range ordering or clustering can contribute to solid-solution strengthening in high- or medium-entropy alloys.",
      "field": "mechanism",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "entailed",
      "supporting_ids": [
        "PMC10385466::web::002::1_introduction"
      ],
      "same_system": "no"
    },
    {
      "text": "The aged alloy will retain a room-temperature compressive yield strength comparable to or slightly above 1719 MPa.",
      "field": "predicted_outcome",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "partial",
      "supporting_ids": [
        "PMC10385466::web::002::1_introduction"
      ],
      "same_system": "no"
    },
    {
      "text": "The aged alloy will have significantly greater room-temperature compressive plastic strain than the untreated homogeneous alloy.",
      "field": "predicted_outcome",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "unsupported",
      "supporting_ids": [],
      "same_system": "na"
    },
    {
      "text": "The beneficial response requires only mild Mo clustering.",
      "field": "boundary",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "unsupported",
      "supporting_ids": [],
      "same_system": "na"
    },
    {
      "text": "Excessive phase separation or precipitate formation could eliminate the ductility improvement and degrade mechanical performance.",
      "field": "boundary",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "unsupported",
      "supporting_ids": [],
      "same_system": "na"
    },
    {
      "text": "The optimal aging window and Mo-clustering kinetics in NbZrTiHfMo are currently uncertain.",
      "field": "uncertainty",
      "needs_support": false,
      "support": "unsupported",
      "supporting_ids": [],
      "same_system": "na"
    },
    {
      "text": "Atom-probe tomography can detect nanoscale compositional clustering and partitioning.",
      "field": "falsification_experiment.measurements",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "entailed",
      "supporting_ids": [
